window.docContents[131].resolve({"/Logic/#Logical-Foundations--Logic-in-Lean--Recap___-Logical-Connectives-in-Lean":{"contents":"Connectives introduced in this chapter:\n\n* a ∧ b (conjunction):* introduced with constructor* eliminated with intro ⟨ha, hb⟩ or obtain ⟨ha, hb⟩ := h* a ∨ b (disjunction):* introduced with left and right* eliminated with cases or obtain h | h := h* False (falsehood):* eliminated with cases or contradiction* ¬ a (negation):* defined as a → False* True (truthhood):* introduced as True.intro or with constructor* a ↔ b (iff):* introduced with constructor* eliminated with intro ⟨hab, hba⟩, obtain ⟨hab, hba⟩ := h, or Iff.mp and Iff.mpr* ∃ x : α, a (existential):* introduced with exists y* eliminated with intro ⟨x, Hx⟩ or obtain ⟨x, Hx⟩ := H\n\nFundamental connectives we've been using since the beginning:\n\n* equality (x = y)* implication (a → b)* universal quantification (∀ x, a)\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Logic in Lean","header":"8.4. Recap: Logical Connectives in Lean","id":"/Logic/#Logical-Foundations--Logic-in-Lean--Recap___-Logical-Connectives-in-Lean"},"/Poly/#Logical-Foundations--Poly___-Polymorphism-and-Higher-Order-Functions--Polymorphism--Polymorphic-Lists--Exercises":{"contents":"def List.rev {α : Type} (l : List α) : List α :=\n  match l with\n  | .nil => .nil\n  | .cons h t => rev t ++ (.cons h .nil)\n\ntheorem rev_nil {α : Type} : ([] : List α).rev = [] := by rfl\n\ntheorem rev_cons {α : Type} {x : α} {l : List α} :\n    (x :: l).rev = l.rev ++ [x] := by rfl\n\n\nHere are a few simple exercises, just like ones in the Lists chapter,\nfor practice with polymorphism. Complete the proofs below.\nYou will find the following\ncharacterizing lemmas for List.append in Lean standard library to be useful:#check List.nil_append\n#check List.cons_append\nList.cons_append.{u} {α : Type u} {a : α} {as bs : List α} : a :: as ++ bs = a :: (as ++ bs)\nList.nil_append.{u} {α : Type u} (as : List α) : [] ++ as = as\ntheorem append_nil {α : Type} {l : List α} :\n    l ++ [] = l := by\n  solution!\n    induction l with\n    | nil => rw [List.nil_append]\n    | cons _ _ ih => rw [List.cons_append, ih]\n\ntheorem append_assoc {α : Type} {l₁ l₂ l₃ : List α} :\n    l₁ ++ l₂ ++ l₃ = l₁ ++ (l₂ ++ l₃) := by\n  solution!\n    induction l₁ with\n    | nil => rw [List.nil_append, List.nil_append]\n    | cons _ _ ih =>\n      repeat rw [List.cons_append]\n      rw [ih]\n\ntheorem append_length {α : Type} {l₁ l₂ : List α} :\n    (l₁ ++ l₂).length = l₁.length + l₂.length := by\n  solution!\n    induction l₁ with\n    | nil =>\n      rw [List.nil_append, List.length_nil, Nat.zero_add]\n    | cons _ _ ih =>\n      rw [List.length_cons, List.cons_append, List.length_cons, Nat.succ_add, ih]\n\n\nHere are some slightly more interesting ones...theorem reverse_append {α : Type} {l₁ l₂ : List α} :\n    (l₁ ++ l₂).rev = l₂.rev ++ l₁.rev := by\n  solution!\n    induction l₁ with\n    | nil =>\n      rw [List.nil_append, rev_nil, append_nil]\n    | cons _ _ ih =>\n      rw [List.cons_append, rev_cons, rev_cons, ih, append_assoc]\n\ntheorem reverse_reverse {α : Type} (l : List α) :\n    l.rev.rev = l := by\n  solution!\n    induction l with\n    | nil => rw [rev_nil, rev_nil]\n    | cons _ _ ih =>\n      rw [rev_cons, reverse_append, ih, rev_cons, rev_nil]\n      rw [List.nil_append, List.cons_append, List.nil_append]\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Poly: Polymorphism and Higher-Order Functions\u0009Polymorphism\u0009Polymorphic Lists","header":"6.1.1.3. Exercises","id":"/Poly/#Logical-Foundations--Poly___-Polymorphism-and-Higher-Order-Functions--Polymorphism--Polymorphic-Lists--Exercises"}});